WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.255
Lesson 8.1.

00:00:02.255 --> 00:00:04.430
DeFi portfolio construction.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.862
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:09.700
to split capital into risk buckets with caps, so

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.075
no single failure can sink the portfolio.

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:14.665
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:16.350
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.065
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.065 --> 00:00:20.590
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.752
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:28.379
First, Buckets: liquidity reserve · core (simple, durable) ·

00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:33.787
productive (LP, vaults, carry) · speculative (new, points, experiments).

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:36.711
Next, Concentration caps: per protocol, per

00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:39.735
chain, per stablecoin issuer, per bridge.

00:00:39.735 --> 00:00:43.419
Then, Genuine diversification: two front ends on the

00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:46.755
same protocol, or two stablecoins with the same

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:49.210
backing, are one risk, not two.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.150
And finally, Rebalancing rules: thresholds that

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.416
trigger moving money between buckets.

00:00:55.716 --> 00:00:58.377
Rebalance when any bucket drifts more than 5

00:00:58.377 --> 00:01:01.161
points from target, or after any incident.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:04.451
Reserve, 15%, Stablecoins split across

00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:07.366
2 issuers, instant access, n/a.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:10.892
Core, 45%, Blue-chip stable lending

00:01:10.892 --> 00:01:14.326
(2 protocols), ETH staking, 20%.

00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:18.219
Productive, 30%, Wide concentrated LP,

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:20.416
a vault, a PT, 10%.

00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:24.931
Speculative, ≤10%, Points, new protocols, 5%.

00:01:26.231 --> 00:01:27.691
Here's your checklist.

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:29.226
Do it now, for real.

00:01:29.226 --> 00:01:31.551
First, Buckets and targets written.

00:01:31.551 --> 00:01:35.226
Next, Caps per protocol, chain, issuer, bridge written.

00:01:35.226 --> 00:01:37.501
And finally, Rebalancing rule written.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.011
Question 1.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:43.731
Two stablecoins backed by the same collateral: diversified?

00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:50.866
The answer: No. They share one failure point.

00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:53.411
Question 2.

00:01:53.411 --> 00:01:54.976
Why keep a reserve bucket?

00:01:59.396 --> 00:02:01.394
The answer: To defend debt, meet

00:02:01.394 --> 00:02:03.936
needs and redeploy without forced selling.

00:02:05.236 --> 00:02:06.506
Question 3.

00:02:06.506 --> 00:02:07.791
When should you rebalance?

00:02:12.211 --> 00:02:14.334
The answer: When buckets drift past

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.456
the threshold, or after an incident.

00:02:17.756 --> 00:02:19.001
Let's recap.

00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:22.220
Buckets: liquidity reserve · core (simple,

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.066
durable) · productive (LP, vaults.

00:02:25.066 --> 00:02:28.005
Concentration caps: per protocol, per chain,

00:02:28.005 --> 00:02:30.526
per stablecoin issuer, per bridge.

00:02:30.526 --> 00:02:34.996
Genuine diversification: two front ends on the same protocol.

00:02:34.996 --> 00:02:39.251
Rebalancing rules: thresholds that trigger moving money between buckets.

00:02:40.551 --> 00:02:43.066
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:46.491
Next up, Lesson 8.2: The DeFi risk framework.
